  "goodToKnow": "Die Haube is a bonnet or cap: die Haube einer Krankenschwester (nurse's cap), the hood of a car (die Motorhaube), a cooker hood (Dunstabzugshaube) and a hairdresser's dryer hood (Trockenhaube). Married women once wore a Haube, hence unter die Haube kommen (to get married). In Austria, top restaurants receive Hauben (toques) from Gault&Millau. Plural: die Hauben."
